Karkov, whose full name is Yuri Karkov, was a human [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Duskwalker|Duskwalker]] of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] and a general of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. He was an older man with blue skin, and he wore the deep blue uniform of the First House. Many people who agreed with him followed him, and he had taken all three of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] bloods at once. [[Org/Althane/The Weft|The Weft]] killed him at [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] took and remade his body.

He raised two children as his wards, the elven woman called [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|the Slipseer]] and the orc [[People/Althane/Rampart|Rampart]] her brother, and kept them as his lieutenants. A locket in his desk holds their portraits as children. Both died before him. He held one of the few ultraviolet keycards to RC3, the installation he ran with [[People/Althane/Natalia|Natalia]].

He was the First House's partner in [[People/Althane/Ezekiel Grimm|Grimm]]'s work in [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/Haven/index|Haven]], drawing power with him from the corpse of the Thessian Beast. When the Weft made war on Grimm, Karkov beat them, showed that he held Tenno's orb, took [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]] and [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] out of the Weft's orb, leaving it an empty shell, and teleported back to Oresk. Earlier he had shot [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] with a weapon whose wound the Broker could not heal while Karkov lived or the weapon survived.

He named the Weft the mongrels who killed his people, broke the beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] the House kept, and their faces went out in flyers across Oresk to be hunted down and hanged in the streets.

During the crisis at RC3 the Deep pressed on his mind, trying to drag him down into slumber. He meant to fight it, and his wounds closed under a black silk like the one [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]] binds with. When the Weft killed him there, [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] shot him with the gun, which stripped his divinity from him, and [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] disintegrated the lower half of his body. Before the Weft could take the corpse, a portal opened and tendrils of the Deep dragged what was left through it.

The Deep remade him into a fungal body grown over the ruin of his own: blue skin under yellow, purple and green growth, three legs splayed radial from a torso cut off where the fungus took it, and little left of him in the mind. He was bent over a great fungus organ at the top of the [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|City of Yellow]], playing without pause, moved not by his own will but by tendrils run from the Deep's hands to his body. He was destroyed with the Deep when the Weft tore the god apart at the top of the hill; what was left of him burned to soot.
